figdown 0.1 block
# The DEFAULT invocation, and the one the hold matters most for. With no
# --color-means the tool cannot classify color=, so it must not migrate
# anything else either: `boundary` → `external` and `w=` → `width=` are the
# very spellings refusal (b) reads to decide the file is too old to be a
# pre-release document. Apply them here and a later --color-means=text run
# has nothing left to refuse — it deletes a FILL and reports success.
node a "A" color=#dbeafe
boundary e "Upstream"
edge a -> e
